Hi Colin --

"colin davenport" <colindaven at gmail.com> writes:

> Dear EBImage users
>[SNIP]
> I used these instructions to install R and bioconductor
> http://hocuspokus.net/2008/05/07/installing-r-bioconductor-on-ubuntu-804/

>From a quick parse of this file it looks like the expectation is that
R and its packages are installed as root. This sounds like a bad idea,
or at least it seems like you'd like to install packages into a
user-defined directory, e.g., using an environment variable R_LIBS, as
discussed in the "R Installation and Administration" page

http://cran.fhcrc.org/doc/manuals/R-admin.html

> One thing .. the bioconductor flagged up errors with the following packages
> affy
> annaffy
> affyPLM

You've installed on top of a previous installation, and so need to
update.packages. See the instructions on

http://bioconductor.org/download

i.e., in a new R session

> source("http://bioconductor.org/biocLite.R")
> update.packages(repos=biocinstallRepos(), ask=FALSE)

Martin

> Thanks for your help !
> Colin
